Starting AssetCooker...
Command line options are:
   --help  : Show this text and stop

   --cores <n> : Use at most n additional cores
   --no_mt <n> : Use to disable multithreading (this stabilizes blp result across runs)
   --platform  <name> : Specify platform to cook for.  Known platforms are:
                          Windows
                          iOS
                          MacOS
                          Linux
                          XBone
                          Switch
                          PS4
                          Stadia
   --mode  <mode> : Specify mode to use cooker in.  Known modes are:
                          XLP
                          ArtDef
                          Dependency

   --pantry <path> : Specify root directory for assets.
                Argument is a relative path from the current 
                  working directory to the package location
                  default is ../pantry 

   --stewpot <path> : Specify root directory for BLP outputs.
                Argument is a relative path from the current 
                  working directory to the BLP location
                  Default is ./BLP 

   --banquet_hall <path> : Specify root directory for cooked ArtDefs.
                Argument is a relative path from the current 
                  working directory to the cooked ArtDefs location
                  default is ./ArtDefs 

   --dependency_root <path> : Specify root directory for cooked Dependency Files.
                Argument is a relative path from the current 
                  working directory to the cooked Dependency File location
                  Default is current working directory.

   --config <path> : Specify name of project config file.
                Argument is a relative path from the current 
                  working directory to the config file
                  Default is ./Config.cfg

   --layout <name> : Use a particular disk layout module.

   --cores <n>  : Change temp heap size to n MB (default: 64)

   --log_sizes  : Print verbose BLP statistics to the log.

   --log_path <path> : Specify directory for logging.
                Argument can be relative or absolute 
                  Logging is disabled if no directory is specified 

  Anything that is not a command line option is taken to be
   a relative path to an XLP or ArtDef depending on mode.
